---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import portrait from '../../ashmit-profile.jpg';
import ProteinComparison from '../components/ProteinComparison.astro';
import ValidationExcerpt from '../components/ValidationExcerpt.astro';
---
<Layout>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="introduction">
      <div>
        <p class="affiliation">Computer Science · NYU Abu Dhabi</p>
        <h1>Ashmit Mukherjee</h1>
        <p>I’m interested in computational social science, especially how AI advice affects decisions people make together.</p>
        <p>I’m a Computer Science senior at NYU Abu Dhabi. I coordinate software development and review for cooperation experiments, and train and evaluate protein language models.</p>
        <div class="intro-links"><a href="mailto:asm8879@nyu.edu">asm8879@nyu.edu</a><a href="https://github.com/Ansester" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a></div>
      </div>
      <Image class="portrait" src={portrait} alt="Ashmit Mukherjee" width={144} height={144} format="webp" loading="eager" />
    </header>

    <section class="research-stories" id="research" aria-labelledby="research-heading">
      <div class="section-label" id="projects"><h2 id="research-heading">Research</h2><span>Two ongoing collaborations</span></div>
      <article class="research-story">
        <div class="story-copy">
          <p class="byline">With Ben Rosche &amp; Hanan Salam · 2026–present</p>
          <h3><a href="/work/human-ai-collaboration/">Human–AI collaboration</a></h3>
          <p class="research-question">How does AI advice affect cooperation when individual and group incentives differ?</p>
          <p>I coordinate development and review whether the software follows the study requirements. My work includes checking that an adviser’s recommendation, the action executed by the game, and the recorded outcome agree.</p>
          <p>The check shown here uses scripted advisers to test the software’s handling of a corrupted result.</p>
          <a class="read-link" href="/work/human-ai-collaboration/">The software and my contribution</a>
        </div>
        <ValidationExcerpt />
      </article>
      <article class="research-story protein-story">
        <div class="story-copy">
          <p class="byline">Co-first author · eBRAIN Lab · 2026–present</p>
          <h3><a href="/work/protein-language-models/">Bio-LoRA &amp; protein-model evaluation</a></h3>
          <p class="research-question">Can biological information help adapt a protein language model?</p>
          <p>I added signal-peptide prediction to the evaluation and compared three ESM-2 model sizes. On SP5, feature injection had the highest mean exact cleavage-site match at 650M; full fine-tuning led at 150M and 3B.</p>
          <a class="read-link" href="/work/protein-language-models/">My contribution and comparison results</a>
        </div>
        <ProteinComparison />
      </article>
      <div class="manuscript-entry" id="manuscript"><span>Manuscript</span><p><cite>Bio-LoRA: Biological Priors as Inductive Bias for Low-Rank Adaptation.</cite><br />Co-first author. Unpublished manuscript, 2026.<br /><a href="/work/protein-language-models/#the-manuscript">About the manuscript and my contribution</a></p></div>
    </section>

    <section class="current-direction" aria-labelledby="direction-heading">
      <h2 id="direction-heading">Current direction</h2>
      <div><h3><a href="/work/synthetic-pilot-lab/">Synthetic Pilot Lab</a></h3><p>My capstone examines how faults in experimental software distort recorded outcomes. The implementation pairs correct and faulty game engines, replays scripted decisions, and checks the resulting records with an independent evaluator.</p><p class="note">Offline diagnostics and measurement analysis completed using synthetic data. Model-based fault discovery remains untested.</p></div>
    </section>

    <section class="other-work" aria-labelledby="other-heading"><h2 id="other-heading">Other projects</h2><p><a href="/work/fieldlens/">FieldLens</a>, a local tool for reviewing fictional incident records; <a href="/work/hinglish-ner/">Hinglish named-entity recognition</a>; and <a href="/work/camp/">CAMP</a>, a team-built campus equipment application.</p><a class="read-link" href="/work/">Projects and coursework</a></section>

    <section class="about-section" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
      <h2 id="about-heading">A little background</h2>
      <div id="background"><p>I’m majoring in Computer Science with a minor in Economics and expect to graduate in May 2027. I’m preparing for doctoral research and am interested in applying computation to social, economic, and historical questions.</p><p>I studied away at NYU Paris and NYU New York. On campus, I’ve facilitated workshops for first-year students and worked front of house at the Arts Center.</p><p id="experience">Previously, I was an ML engineering intern at Zeek (summer 2025), working on customer segmentation and model comparison.</p></div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
